# Playwright Hybrid Automation Framework (API + UI Integration)

An end-to-end test automation framework built with **Playwright** and **JavaScript**, implementing a **Hybrid E2E Strategy** to optimize execution speed and stability.

---

## 📌 Key Architectural Highlights

* **API Preconditions**: Offloads heavy setup workflows (Account Creation & User Login) to background API requests (`beforeAll` hook).
* **Dynamic CSRF & Authentication**: Automates CSRF middleware token extraction and injects cookies directly into headers.
* **State Preservation**: Saves authenticated browser context into `state.json` (`storageState`), bypassing slow UI authentication forms.
* **Page Object Model (POM)**: Modularity and maintenance-friendly design separating locators and actions from test scripts.
* **Data-Driven Approach**: Externalized test data parameters using JSON configuration files.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Automation Tool:** Playwright
* **Language:** JavaScript (Node.js)
* **Architecture:** Page Object Model (POM)
* **Design Pattern:** Hybrid (API Setup + UI Functional Validation)
* **Reporting:** Allure Reporter / Playwright HTML Reporter

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1️⃣ Prerequisites
Ensure you have [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) installed on your machine.

### 2️⃣ Installation
Clone the repository and install dependencies:
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/MoameniBrahim-sys/Playwright-Hybrid-API-UI-Framework.git](https://github.com/MoameniBrahim-sys/Playwright-Hybrid-API-UI-Framework.git)
cd Playwright-Hybrid-API-UI-Framework
npm install

3️⃣ Running Tests
Execute the E2E test suite in headless mode:

Bash
npx playwright test
Execute tests in UI/Headed mode:

Bash
npx playwright test --headed
4️⃣ Generate Reports
Generate and view the Allure execution report:

Bash
npx playwright test --reporter=allure-playwright
npx allure serve allure-results
